  "seoBody": "<h3 data-short=\"No\">Do I need a new app?</h3><p>Do you have WhatsApp? No new app needed. Do you have Telegram? No new app needed. Have neither? Time to join the more than 3 billion people on WhatsApp, or the more than 1 billion on Telegram.</p><h3 data-short=\"It's processed\">What happens when I say done?</h3><p>Saying done is how Quickler knows your inspection is finished. Then it processes everything you sent. You read the report, change any word, and send it.</p><h3 data-short=\"Yes\">Can it fill in my own report?</h3><p>Yes. Send a finished report in Word or PDF. Every new one comes back in that layout, with your headings, tables and logo.</p><h3 data-short=\"Yes\">Can the AI get it wrong?</h3><p>It can. So nothing is filed until you say done, and anything it cannot settle is raised with you, not guessed. Quickler knows only what is said in that chat, plus your Check. If you did not say it, Quickler will not make it up.</p><h3 data-short=\"To do list\">What happens to Faults?</h3><p>Each Fault is listed with its place. Each one becomes a job on the To do list.</p><h3 data-short=\"As big as you need\">How big can a report be?</h3><p>As big as you need.</p><h3 data-short=\"80 to 90%\">How much time does it save?</h3><p>Currently an 80 to 90% cut in desk time. We are aiming for 100%, and we have been improving by 8% a week.</p><h3 data-short=\"EU\">Where are records stored?</h3><p>On EU servers. You can download or delete records on request.</p><h3 data-short=\"Yes\">Is Quickler GDPR compliant?</h3><p>Quickler is registered with the Information Commission (formerly the ICO), ZC124993. Data is held on EU servers under a Data Processing Agreement.</p><h3 data-short=\"You\">Who owns the data?</h3><p>You do. Quickler is the processor and you are the controller. If you leave, you can download every record and we delete our copy.</p><h3 data-short=\"Yes\">Can I download records?</h3><p>Yes, any time, as PDF, Word, Excel, CSV or a web page.</p>",
